# A CRLF line ending after a shebang makes the kernel fail to find the
# interpreter, so "no such file or directory" is the only error you get. This
# repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which means the
# working copy gets CRLF unless told otherwise. The pre-commit guard is a
# POSIX shell script, so it is pinned to LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
